{
  "title": "The new Hijri year",
  "pages": "69",
  "intro": "The Muslim year starts on 1 Muharram and remembers the Hijrah.",
  "learn": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "html": "The new Muslim year begins on the <b>1st of Muharram</b>. On this day we remember the <b>Hijrah</b>, so we call this year the <b>Hijri</b> year. The Hijrah is the move of Muhammad (SAW) and the Muslims from <b>Makkah to Madinah</b>. It happened in <b>622</b>, and since then Muslims count their years by the Hijri calendar."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The twelve months of the Hijri calendar"
